			"text": "HTTP ",
			"fontSize": 33.81952121956242,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "HTTP ",
			"autoResize": true,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "q3JgztRt",
			"type": "text",
			"x": -699.8767944132893,
			"y": 43.838312166151184,
			"width": 980.4388290669483,
			"height": 242.03674868645498,
			"angle": 0,
			"strokeColor": "#1e1e1e",
			"backgroundColor": "transparent",
			"fillStyle": "solid",
			"strokeWidth": 1,
			"strokeStyle": "solid",
			"roughness": 1,
			"opacity": 100,
			"groupIds": [
				"Q1T8Z8u4MUTzL8kqR1Ux1"
			],
			"frameId": null,
			"index": "b8wV",
			"roundness": null,
			"seed": 2036877943,
			"version": 1711,
			"versionNonce": 1177526265,
			"isDeleted": false,
			"boundElements": [],
			"updated": 1759771502828,
			"link": null,
			"locked": false,
			"text": "2. Client Server Modal \n\n- Client Initiates the connection with Server and server then sends data to client.\n- For this we need a connection which is managed by TCP which is one of two most common transport\nprotocols i.e UDP and TCP\n- TCP is more reliable and uses Three way handsahke ( client sends a connection initiating request,\nserver responds with acknowlegde and then client again responds with acknowledge )\n- Request and Response have headers which allow different layers of network ( OSI model ) to help\nthem navigate the body / content to reach its destination without exploring the content of the\nrequest or response.",
			"fontSize": 19.3629398949164,
			"fontFamily": 5,
			"textAlign": "left",
			"verticalAlign": "top",
			"containerId": null,
			"originalText": "2. Client Server Modal \n\n- Client Initiates the connection with Server and server then sends data to client.\n- For this we need a connection which is managed by TCP which is one of two most common transport\nprotocols i.e UDP and TCP\n- TCP is more reliable and uses Three way handsahke ( client sends a connection initiating request,\nserver responds with acknowlegde and then client again responds with acknowledge )\n- Request and Response have headers which allow different layers of network ( OSI model ) to help\nthem navigate the body / content to reach its destination without exploring the content of the\nrequest or response.",
			"autoResize": false,
			"lineHeight": 1.25,
			"hasTextLink": false,
			"rawText": ""
		},
		{
			"id": "Esbs_r-ttsSWZql0U_2eO",
